\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1.2 The posture rule (very important)\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
STAND and SIT are 
\f0\b one and the same command
\f1\b0  (0x21010202) \'97 a 
\f0\b toggle
\f1\b0 . Sending it while already standing makes the robot sit, and vice versa.\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Actions that need a specific pose declare it ("posture": "sit" or "stand"). The console only re-poses when it knows the state is wrong; with "force_posture": true it re-poses even when the state is unknown (used for rolls/jumps).\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The posture tracker resets on restart, so after starting the app: put the robot in the pose you want (or let the action's own pose step do it) and press the button.\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Velocity/driving commands are only honoured while the robot is 
\f0\b standing
\f1\b0 ; while sitting they are ignored silently.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1.3 Adding or editing a command (config.json)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Each button is one entry under "actions". Example:\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 "twist_jump": \{\
  "enabled": true,\
  "note": "twist jump (0x2101020D - standing, moves dog)",\
  "posture": "stand",\
  "force_posture": true,\
  "replay": "slow",\
  "group": "action",\
  "icon": "\uc0\u55356 \u57130 \u65039 ",\
  "label": "Twist jump",\
  "frame": \{ "code": "0x2101020D", "type": 0, "value": 0 \}\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
frame.code \'97 the 32-bit command (hex). type 0 = simple frame; value \'97 integer parameter (velocity frames use payload instead).\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
posture / force_posture \'97 pose handling as above. Omit for actions valid in any pose.\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
replay: "slow" \'97 sends the frame three times at ~1 Hz (used for poses/rolls). "once": true \'97 a single frame (used for mode/gait switches). Default \'97 short burst.\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
group \'97 which block the button appears in (recovery / action / mode / gait). icon + label \'97 button face; note \'97 tooltip.\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
After editing: restart the console (or reload the page) \'97 buttons appear automatically. Disable a button with "enabled": false.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1.4 Finding the right code for a new command\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	1	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Probe:
\f1\b0  Advanced \uc0\u8594  raw frames \'97 send a frame once and watch the robot.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	2	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Capture from the official remote:
\f1\b0  run tools/retroid_listen.py on the console computer, point the RETROID controlapp at <console IP>:12121, press the button there, and read the exact frame.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	3	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Safety:
\f1\b0  test new poses on a soft surface with clear space; keep the physical E-stop in reach. E-STOP in the console cancels any action mid-play and blocks all commands until \uc0\u10226  Return.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 2. Two-joystick movement\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 2.1 Layout\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Left stick
\f1\b0  \'97 up/down = forward/back \'b7 left/right = turn.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Right stick
\f1\b0  \'97 left/right = slide (side-walk) \'b7 up/down = forward/back (if both sticks push forward, the stronger one wins).\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Diagonals combine axes (e.g. forward + slide, or forward + turn).\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Both sticks are 
\f0\b spring-centred
\f1\b0 : release = knob returns to centre and the robot stops (a brake frame is sent immediately).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 2.2 Stopping\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Release either stick (or return it to centre) \uc0\u8594  stop.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
STOP
\f1\b0  button \uc0\u8594  official brake frames. 
\f0\b E-STOP
\f1\b0  \uc0\u8594  latches until \u10226  Return.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Switching browser tab / losing window focus also stops the robot (safety).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 2.3 Sensitivity and speed (Advanced)\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Stick curve
\f1\b0  \'97 Linear / Soft (default) / Soft+: higher curve = finer control near the centre.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Speed scale
\f1\b0  \'97 50 % / 75 % / 100 % / 150 %: multiplies the configured maxima (defaults: 0.5 m/s forward, 0.4 m/s lateral, 0.8 rad/s turn).\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Forward / Turn / Lateral sign
\f1\b0  \'97 flips each axis if a direction feels reversed; applied instantly.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Joystick mode
\f1\b0  \'97 
\f3\i Velocity frames
\f1\i0  (proven) or 
\f3\i Retroid / official SDK
\f1\i0  (sends the same 42-byte frames as the physical remote to UDP 12121).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 2.4 Keyboard (alternative to the sticks)\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
W / S
\f1\b0  (or \uc0\u8593 /\u8595 ) \'97 forward / back \'b7 
\f0\b A / D
\f1\b0  (or \uc0\u8592 /\u8594 ) \'97 turn \'b7 
\f0\b Space
\f1\b0  \'97 E-stop (hold) \'b7 leaving the keys stops the robot.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 3. Camera setup\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf0 3.1 How the video path works\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The console asks the robot to start its camera services (command 0x21012109, value 0x40, to UDP 43899) and reads the stream at rtsp://<robot IP>:8554/test, re-publishing it to the browser as MJPEG.\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Feed opens automatically after connecting and is kept open by a watchdog that retries every ~8 s (re-sending the start command, reconnecting the stream).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 3.2 If the robot publishes nothing (RTSP 404 / no video)\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	1	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Confirm the robot is on and reachable: ping 192.168.2.1 (robot Wi-Fi) or 192.168.1.120 (LAN).\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	2	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Check the RTSP port is open and whether the stream name exists:\uc0\u8232 nc -z -w2 192.168.2.1 8554\u8232 ffprobe -v error -rtsp_transport tcp -show_entries format=format_name -of csv=p=0 rtsp://192.168.2.1:8554/test\u8232 A working stream prints rtsp; "404 Not Found" means the camera service on the robot is not publishing.\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	3	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
If the port is open but the stream is absent, the robot's camera service must be started on the robot (its own service/tooling); power-cycling the robot usually restores it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 3.3 Tuning quality for a stable feed (Advanced \uc0\u8594  Camera stream)\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
FPS
\f1\b0  \'97 4\'966 fps is plenty for driving (lower = lighter).\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Scale
\f1\b0  \'97 e.g. 480:-1 (default, light) or 640:-1 (sharper, heavier); 320:-1 for the lowest bandwidth.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Quality
\f1\b0  \'97 MJPEG -q:v: 2 = best/largest, 18 = smallest; default 11 balances both.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Apply & restart camera
\f1\b0  \'97 applies immediately; 
\f0\b Camera off
\f1\b0  stops the feed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Rule of thumb: if the picture stutters on the robot's Wi-Fi, lower FPS first, then scale, then raise the quality number.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3\i \cf0 Ports:
\f1\i0  commands 43893 (UDP) \'b7 telemetry 43897 (UDP) \'b7 camera control 43899 (UDP) \'b7 RTSP 8554 (TCP, /test) \'b7 remote 12121 (UDP) \'b7 console 8123 (HTTP).\
